scenario ser-error-deferred-to-commit
title "Serializable: the error comes at commit, not at the next statement"
story "T1 and T2 depend on each other; T1 commits, so T2 can no longer commit. This engine aborts T2 at its next statement. PostgreSQL raises no error before T2 rolls back by itself. If T2 commits instead, PostgreSQL aborts T2 at the commit."
schedule:
  T2 BEGIN
  T2 SCAN q: AS v2_0
  T2 PUT p:1 = 1
  T1 BEGIN
  T1 READ p:1 AS v1_2
  T1 PUT q:2 = 35
  T1 COMMIT
  T2 READ q:1 AS v2_3
  T2 ABORT
